    "title": "First Warning Forecast: Severe weather threat Easter Sunday",
    "text": "WeatherToday's Forecast Actions Facebook Tweet Email First Warning Forecast: Severe weather threat Easter Sunday A strong cold front will bring the chance of isolated strong to severe storms this Easter Sunday. Cooler temperatures return next week. Prev Next By: Derrah Getter Posted 5:09 PM, Apr 04, 2026 Derrah Getter's First Warning ForecastThis evening, skies will be partly cloudy. Lows tonight fall into the mid 60s. Sunday morning will be dry. Sunrise will be at 6:42 am. Clouds increase throughout the morning. Showers and thunderstorms arrive in the afternoon. Highs will reach the upper 70s. There is a level 1 out of 5 severe weather threat in place. Damaging wind gusts will be possible. The line of storms exits the region late Sunday night. Cooler temperatures return for most of next week. Highs will be closer to average in the 50s and 60s. The brief cool down will slightly lower the tree pollen levels. Conditions will be mainly dry. Temperatures start warming up again late week. Let's connect on social media!Forecaster Derrah Getter:For weather updates on Facebook: HEREFor weather updates on X: HEREFollow me on Instagram: HERECheck out the Interactive Radar on WTKR.com: Interactive Radar Recommended For You Marketplace Sell Your Items - Free to List Visit Full Marketplace Gridiron Heritage Two Tone Limited Snapback Hat $30 SportServer P. | sellwild.com University of Texas Football Shirts, Longhorns Football swea... $20 SportServer P. | sellwild.com Ohio State OSU Buckeyes White Spaghetti Tank $36 SportServer P. | sellwild.com Mac Mini (M4 Pro) $990 sellwild.com 2009 Ford Mustang $29,000 Gateway C. | sellwild.com Pearl Necklace $15 Mark M. | sellwild.com Avon Watch $15 Mark M. | sellwild.com Powered by True Crime 757 Podcast",
